{"qid":"Q676745","names":["County of Armagnac"],"title":"County of Armagnac","endonym":{"native":"Armanhac","lang":"oc"},"capsule":"The County of Armagnac was a feudal lordship in Gascony, southwestern France, situated between the Adour and Garonne rivers, formally constituted when the title 'Count of Armagnac' was established around 960 CE. The dynasty rose to regional dominance under Bernard VII (count 1391–1418), who led the Armagnac faction in the French civil war against the Burgundians, serving as constable of France; his assassination in 1418 by Burgundian partisans marked the faction's nadir. The county reached its greatest territorial extent under John V (count 1450–1473), who entered into treasonous correspondence with the English and was expelled by Louis XI. Louis XI abolished the county in 1473, though it briefly reverted to the Albret family before being formally reunited with the French crown in 1497.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. The territorial extent of the County of Armagnac is moderately well attested from feudal charters and French royal administrative records, though precise boundaries shifted considerably across the three centuries of its existence.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: County of Armagnac","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/County_of_Armagnac"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Bernard VII, Count of Armagnac","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bernard_VII,_Count_of_Armagnac"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Armagnac–Burgundian Civil War","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Armagnac%E2%80%93Burgundian_Civil_War"}],"britannica":null,"cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"County of Ar